        "text": "José Luis Solache Jr. has represented the 62nd Assembly District since December 2024. He chairs the Assembly Economic Development, Growth, and Household Impact Committee. Previously, he served on the Lynwood City Council from 2013 to 2024, including as mayor. He spent three terms on the Lynwood Unified School District Board of Education. He also directed government and community relations at the Oldtimers Foundation, a nonprofit serving seniors.",
